  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller (cascade managing)",
  "applies_to": "Boilers with an ebm-papst ArgusVision control acting as the managing (lead) boiler of a cascade, read over Modbus by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for an ArgusVision managing boiler: 78 objects (41 AI, 28 AO, 7 BI, 2 BO), 60 polled by default. On top of the single-boiler block it adds the controller CH/DHW setpoints, outdoor-reset limits, dependent boiler state/status/error and firing rate, controller state/status/error and the cascade firing rate.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile TRIO_MANAGING_BOILER_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the ebm-papst ArgusVision Modbus map (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/ebmModbusspec.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 60 of the 78 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Min Firing Rate); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile TRIO_MANAGING_BOILER_a",
    "doc_number": "TRIO_MANAGING_BOILER_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/TrioManagingBoiler.zip"
  },
